      "writtenOn": "2021-03-29T08:51:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am worried of flakes – I don\u0027t think there are any particular guarantees of executing the messages within any amount of time in Handler, only more than asked. And on this kind of time scale, I would be surprised if we didn\u0027t get some non-negligeable percentage of flakes.\n\nHave you run this in a tight loop a couple hundred times to have a first estimate of the flake rate ?\n\nIf it is flaky, an option would be to make the timer a very long time, and to call the events manually on CS to test the order of the netd commands ; you\u0027d have a separate test for the order of events.\nAnother option would be to have a spy on the agent so you can use it in an inOrder with the netd mock. The check in l.2879 could be hardcoded in onNetworkDisconnected in the instrumented agent since this should be an invariant anyway.",
